Z||000000||Craig||11-20-2001||08:33 AM||||With the clutch pedal in I have a clicking noise in my '86 V6 (40,000 mi on short block). The noise disappears with the clutch pedal out so I thought I had a throw out bearing problem.  A mechanic friend listened to the engine and suggested checking the crankshaft end play.  Mine is about .125" so I think that I need to pull the crankshaft to check it and the thrust bearing.  If this is what I need to do can the crankshaft be pulled out the bottom without pulling the engine?<P>------------------<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||watts||11-20-2001||12:49 PM||||The center thrust bearing can usually be changed out by just dropping the pan and spinning the bearing out.  Assuming you have no crank damage causing the excess slop that is.<P>||||reg||1
